            <div xml:id="d771">

                <pb facs="0886" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg801"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.48/74: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Salvador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Arnold</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-30"><hi rendition="#italic">April 30,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your April 28, and April 29. Express appropriately to Salvadorean Government deep
                    sympathy and regret of Government and <pb facs="0887" n="802" xml:id="pg802"/>
                    people of United States on account of earthquake and hope that loss of life may
                    not be as great as reported. American Red Cross advised of request for 100
                    tents.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
